    fact: "*Ditto*, which Americans say to mean “same here,” comes from an Italian word meaning “said,” as in “the said month.” In Italian it was used in lists of dates so writers didn't have to repeat the name of the month, and the ditto mark, a pair of small quotation marks under a word, still does that job.",
